+## Capping a request body
+
+```ts
+import { bodyLimit } from "@y-core/forge/security";
+
+app.use("/uploads/*", bodyLimit({ maxBytes: 1_048_576 }));
+```
+
+A `Content-Length` over `maxBytes` is refused `413` before the body is read. A body with no `Content-Length`, or one that lies, is counted as it
+streams and refused the moment it passes the cap; a body within it is handed on whole, so the handler reads it as usual. The refusal is
+`{ guard: "body-limit", status: 413, reason: "too-large" }`, answered by `onRefuse`, else the chain's hook, else `Payload Too Large`
+([`FORGE_ERRORS.md`][eh-3e] §3e).
+
+---
